{
  "id": "ss.icon.wand",
  "name": "Acid glob icon",
  "description": "UI slot icon for the spitter. The glyph is not a second drawing of the weapon \u2014 it composes `ss.proj.bolt` itself via `use`, so the icon can never drift from the projectile the way the original i_wand and p_bolt did; when that document stopped being a knapped shell dart and became a drop of acid, this followed with no edit here. Evolved is a rim swap, not a redraw. Rim is `$bile` \u2014 the acid itself, which is what makes this slot findable at a glance.",
  "tags": [
    "icon",
    "weapon"
  ],
  "size": [
    32,
    32
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "id": "tile",
      "shape": {
        "kind": "rect",
        "w": 32,
        "h": 32,
        "corner": 6
      },
      "fill": "$bile"
    },
    {
      "id": "inner",
      "shape": {
        "kind": "rect",
        "w": 28,
        "h": 28,
        "corner": 5
      },
      "fill": "$coal.dark"
    },
    {
      "id": "glyph",
      "use": "ss.proj.bolt",
      "at": [
        -1,
        0
      ],
      "rot": -20,
      "scale": 1.7
    }
  ],
  "variants": {
    "evolved": {
      "description": "Acid Jet. The rim goes gold, and the glob becomes a jet driving forward: one thick stream that comes in flush with the plate's left edge — cut level with it, so it reads as running in from out of frame rather than as a second, longer glob — and surges up and to the right, fattening from 5 to 8.6 toward a blunt round head, the way the weapon's own pour is fattest at the front. It is the glob's own materials, an ink skin, a bile body and a bile.light line down the upper side, so the two slots read as one weapon. What says force is outside it: three beads of spray fanning off the head and two speed streaks alongside. No highlight dot on the head — on a round end that is an eye, and the jet turns into a worm.",
      "set": { "tile.fill": "$gold" },
      "remove": ["glyph"],
